Description: Read a CONNECT response no further than its header
 HttpConnection::receiveResponse() fills its receive buffer with one recv()
 and drains only the response header. A tunnel's next command (FTP
 negotiation, SFTP negotiation, an FTP data connection) is constructed from
 the socket alone, so any bytes of the tunnelled protocol that arrived in
 the same read as the CONNECT response -- a server-first FTP greeting or SSH
 banner -- were silently discarded, and the transfer then timed out waiting
 for them. A CONNECT response is now read byte by byte until its header is
 complete, leaving every following byte on the socket for whatever reads the
 tunnel next. Ordinary HTTP responses are read exactly as before.
Author: DebridPulse <https://github.com/Xipher-Zero/debridpulse>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
